    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n87902" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόκωπος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κώπη</span>) of the sword, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>grasped by the hilt, drawn,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				1651
			</span></i> (troch.), <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Or.</u>
				1477
			</span></i> (lyr.), al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			metaph., <i>ready,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				1652
			</span></i> (troch.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔχειν π. τὴν δεξιάν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdn.
					7.5.4
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>elongated,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>SD</u>
				2.4
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόκοποι</span> codd.); of the
				<i>os uteri, advanced,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				1.34
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προκοπώτερον</span>
		cod.).</div>
